# "Your graveyard" and "named Ancestral Anger": Bot2 casts Ancestral Anger on its own Ornithopter on turn 2, so one is in Bot2's
# graveyard, and Bot1's own graveyard holds a Lightning Bolt (another name). Bot1's Ancestral Anger on turn 3 still has X = 1:
# the Ornithopter ends as a 1/2.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mountain
Lightning Bolt
Ornithopter
Ancestral Anger
Mountain
Island x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Mountain
Ornithopter
Ancestral Anger
Island x11

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mountain.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Mountain.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Lightning Bolt.Cast(Bot2)
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Mountain.Play
Bot2.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot2.Battlefield.Mountain.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Ancestral Anger.Cast(Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter)
Bot2.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Mountain.Play
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mountain.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Ancestral Anger.Cast(Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter)
Bot1.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot2.Graveyard = Ancestral Anger
Bot1.Graveyard = Ancestral Anger; Lightning Bolt
Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Power = 1
